# Tech News Scraper — Architecture & Rules

## Project Overview
Portfolio site (cemkoyluoglu.codes) with a deterministic Turkish→English tech news ingestion pipeline.
Source: nuvemmag.com (Turkish WordPress site)
Stack: Node.js ESM, Vercel Edge Functions, Supabase PostgreSQL, GitHub Actions

### Daily Agent Contract
- Scan only these 6 business categories: `yapay-zeka`, `teknoloji`, `yapay-zeka-uygulamalari`, `gundem`, `surdurulebilirlik`, `bilim-ve-dunya`
- Scrapers discover candidates only
- `scripts/lib/scraper/ScrapeOrchestrator.js` decides which candidates are `today`, `unknown`, `stale` (recent ≤MAX_RECENT_PUBLISH_DAYS / truly stale), or `future`
- Database-first gate must happen before expensive translation/save work
- `unknown` date candidates require detail verification before they can move forward
- `stale` candidates within `SCRAPER_CONFIG.MAX_RECENT_PUBLISH_DAYS` (default 3) are treated as recent and included alongside today candidates
- Future dates must be rejected; when list and detail dates disagree, **detail metadata is canonical only if** it is `today` or `stale` with `ageDays ≤ MAX_RECENT_PUBLISH_DAYS`; otherwise **reject** (avoids saving old articles from mis-tagged list rows). Same rule in `resolveSaveDateIntegrity`.
- Every run must produce a replayable JSON artifact with decision batches

