## Scraper Architecture (OOP)

### Class Hierarchy
```
BaseScraper (abstract)
├── FirecrawlScraper   — Primary scraper via Firecrawl API v2
└── CheerioScraper     — Fallback scraper via fetch + cheerio

ScraperRouter          — Routes between scrapers, handles auto-fallback
```

### File Locations
```
scripts/
├── news-scraper.js                          ← CLI entry point (delegates to ScrapeOrchestrator)
├── lib/scraper/ScrapeOrchestrator.js        ← Active orchestration + decision engine
├── lib/scraper/
│   ├── config.js                            ← All config constants & model names
│   ├── database.js                          ← Supabase ops + duplicate/date save guards
│   ├── dateUtils.js                         ← Turkey-time date normalization/classification
│   ├── translator.js                        ← Translation pipeline
│   └── scrapers/
│       ├── BaseScraper.js                   ← Abstract base class
│       ├── FirecrawlScraper.js              ← Firecrawl API v2 implementation
│       ├── CheerioScraper.js                ← fetch+cheerio implementation
│       └── ScraperRouter.js                 ← Auto-routing + fallback logic
├── embeds/
│   ├── extractEmbeds.js                     ← HTML → embed tokens (cheerio)
│   ├── extractMarkdownEmbeds.js             ← Markdown link → embed tokens
│   └── cleanMarkdownEmbeds.js               ← Clean TikTok/Twitter blockquotes
├── translate/
│   └── prompt.js                            ← All LLM prompts
└── validation/
    ├── contentQualityCheck.js               ← Legacy quality checks
    └── smartArticleProcessor.js             ← Smart validation pipeline
```

### CRITICAL: Orchestration lives in ScrapeOrchestrator
- `news-scraper.js` is CLI glue only
- No scraping logic in news-scraper.js
- No Firecrawl API calls in news-scraper.js
- No cheerio parsing in news-scraper.js
- All scraping goes through ScraperRouter
- Candidate classification, DB-first gating, unknown-date verification, replay, and metrics live here

### Deterministic Run Flow
```text
discover candidates
→ normalize source dates in Turkey time
→ partition into today / unknown / stale / future
→ split stale into recent (≤MAX_RECENT_PUBLISH_DAYS) and truly stale (older)
→ bulk DB check on today + recent + unknown candidates
→ skip existing
→ verify unknown-date candidates with detail metadata
→ translate + validate + save valid missing today + recent articles
→ persist run report artifact
```

