## Date Policy

- Single source of truth: `scripts/lib/scraper/dateUtils.js`
- `normalizeSourceDate()` returns `normalizedDate`, `isoDate`, `dateStatus`, `dateSource`, `dateConfidence`, `datePriority`
- Valid statuses:
  - `today`
  - `unknown`
  - `stale`
  - `future`
- Never silently fall back unknown dates to today
- Save-time date integrity check in `database.js` must compare discovery vs detail date when both exist
- Turkey timezone is `Europe/Istanbul` for all candidate/date decisions

### Recent Article Window (`MAX_RECENT_PUBLISH_DAYS` in `scripts/lib/scraper/config.js`, default 3)
- NuvemMag lists newest first; list scraping uses the first archive page only (`CATEGORY_ARCHIVE_MAX_PAGES: 1`) and a modest per-category cap
- Stale candidates within that window are treated as "recent" and included in the actionable queue
- Discovery vs detail date mismatch: detail page metadata is canonical (see `getProcessingDateDecision`); recent window applies to stale/recent classification
- `verifyUnknownCandidates()` accepts recent articles (not just today) via `isRecentEnough`
- Articles older than the window are skipped at partition level

