## Observability & Replay

- Every scraper run writes a JSON artifact under `artifacts/tech-news-runs/`
- Core metrics tracked per run: `rawFound`, `todayCandidates`, `recentStaleCandidates`, `unknownCandidates`, `alreadyInDb`, `verifiedUnknown`, `staleSkipped`, `futureRejected`, `rejectedDateMismatch`, `saved`, `failed`, `deferred`
- Batch details are grouped into `saved`, `skipped`, `rejected`, `failed`, and `deferred`
- Replay command: `npm run scrape:news:replay -- --replay-file <artifact-path>`
- Supported replay batches: `rejected`, `failed`, `deleted`, `deferred`, `skipped`
- Cleanup scripts also snapshot deleted rows into the same artifact directory so bad/deleted batches can be replayed later
- Replay is not a repair tool while the conflicting `source_url` row still exists in DB

